## Execution

The requested-base diff stat is 25 files, +160/−3467. Package-scoped build, regular vet, and integration-tagged vet passed with `CGO_ENABLED=0`. The CGO-enabled build hit sandbox-denied Xcode temporary-file writes.

The attribution unit tests passed; `go tool cover` reported 100% for `RepoAttributionCountsFromStats` and `ObserveRepoAttribution`. Analytics tests passed with 90.0% coverage; `LatestWorkUnitRepoEffortSource` was 100% and `resolveSankeyCoverage` 88.2%. The broader investment and jobruntime test runs produced coverage profiles but failed where tests tried to bind local `httptest` listeners (`operation not permitted`). I read the profiles; the materializer run/log path was not covered by those runs.

The container-backed behavior proof was not run here. Handoff to bigboy via the oci-image recipe:

```bash
go test -tags=integration -count=1 -run '^TestNoTeamOwnershipRepositoryFallbackProviderEntityMatrix$' ./internal/jobs/investment
go test -tags=integration -count=1 -run '^TestResolveSankeyCoverage_SeededRealClickHouse_SplitPartitionsExactly$' ./internal/queryapi/analytics
```

No Docker or service was used. The sandbox denied deleting the generated Go cache, so `.codex-review-tmp/` remains untracked.

## Question (verbatim)

> what does this change make observable, and what regression in it would be invisible at Info?

It makes unattributed allocation visible as a NULL-repository `empty` row for zero effort or an `active_hours_unassigned` row carrying the full active-hours effort. The per-run Info record reports the four repository-resolution buckets: own, ancestor, children, and unassigned. A persistence or reader regression after that classification—such as dropped unassigned hours or a stale `team_ownership` generation being selected—would be invisible at Info because the log records pre-write classification, not persisted rows or readback totals.

